    <item>
      <title>Kumbhakarna&apos;s Downfall</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the golden age of the Ramayana, Ravana, the mighty king of Lanka, and his loyal brother Kumbhakarna ruled their kingdom with unparalleled power. But when the great sage Vishvamitra arrived in Lanka, he prophesied the impending doom of the kingdom, foretelling the invasion of the monkey army. Ravana, in his wisdom, heeded the warning and began preparing his army for war. But Kumbhakarna, blinded by his insatiable sleep, remained complacent and ignored the danger. He slept through the war, believing the gods would protect him. But when the monkey army arrived, the gods were nowhere to be seen, and Kumbhakarna finally woke to find his kingdom in chaos. His people were fleeing, his brother Ravana was fighting for his life, and the enemy was at their gates. Kumbhakarna rushed to join the battle, but it was too late. The monkey army had already broken through the gates, and the kingdom was lost. This is Sloth — the refusal to act when danger looms, and the price of inaction is paid in blood. Today we sleep through the alarms of our own lives, and the consequences are devastating.</description>
